WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.278 --> 00:00:03.256
Once the decision is clear and you have begun

2
00:00:03.278 --> 00:00:08.100
gathering relevant perspectives, compare more than one practical option.

3
00:00:08.478 --> 00:00:11.011
Include the current approach when it is a meaningful

4
00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:14.744
alternative. A comparison helps you see what each choice

5
00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:17.744
makes easier, what it may make harder and what

6
00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:18.922
you still need to learn.

7
00:00:19.509 --> 00:00:24.176
For the reminder example, consider three possibilities: keep mail

8
00:00:24.198 --> 00:00:27.464
as it is; replace mail with text only; or

9
00:00:27.487 --> 00:00:29.798
offer more than one method with a usable route

10
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.042
for help. These are options for analysis, not a

11
00:00:33.064 --> 00:00:36.176
claim that every option is permitted, approved or ready

12
00:00:36.198 --> 00:00:36.820
to implement.

13
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.387
Before recommending any of them, confirm the requirements, decision

14
00:00:41.409 --> 00:00:45.076
authority and resources. Where additional information or review is

15
00:00:45.098 --> 00:00:48.098
needed, mark that need rather than presenting a preference

16
00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.409
as an approved plan.

17
00:00:50.464 --> 00:00:53.487
A text message might be convenient for someone who

18
00:00:53.509 --> 00:00:56.131
can receive and use it. Mail might be more

19
00:00:56.153 --> 00:00:59.020
accessible or private for another person in a particular

20
00:00:59.042 --> 00:01:03.509
situation. Multiple methods may support choice but require staff

21
00:01:03.531 --> 00:01:07.264
time, reliable contact information and a plan to maintain

22
00:01:07.287 --> 00:01:07.953
each option.

23
00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:12.957
These possibilities need inquiry. Do not assign a communication

24
00:01:12.979 --> 00:01:17.446
preference to someone based on identity, disability, language, income

25
00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:20.823
or age. Ask what the available evidence and appropriate

26
00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:24.690
engagement reveal, and identify whose experience is still missing.

27
00:01:25.346 --> 00:01:29.546
Consider burdens as well as benefits. Does an option

28
00:01:29.568 --> 00:01:33.057
ask a person to obtain a device, navigate a

29
00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:36.990
difficult process, share information they would rather keep private

30
00:01:37.012 --> 00:01:39.768
or find help on their own? Does it increase

31
00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:42.190
effort for staff or partners in a way that

32
00:01:42.212 --> 00:01:42.946
needs planning?

33
00:01:44.058 --> 00:01:47.280
Feasibility includes more than whether a method can be

34
00:01:47.302 --> 00:01:50.569
purchased or launched. Check whether the information can be

35
00:01:50.591 --> 00:01:55.236
delivered accessibly, whether language assistance and disability-related needs can

36
00:01:55.258 --> 00:01:58.391
be addressed, and whether the relevant offices can support

37
00:01:58.413 --> 00:01:59.547
the proposed process.

38
00:02:00.113 --> 00:02:05.313
Also consider timing, resources, maintenance, privacy and what happens

39
00:02:05.336 --> 00:02:08.180
when a message is not received. A backup route

40
00:02:08.202 --> 00:02:11.313
matters. A choice can be technically possible and still

41
00:02:11.336 --> 00:02:13.536
leave a person without a usable next step.

42
00:02:14.124 --> 00:02:17.524
Do not invent costs, response rates or access needs

43
00:02:17.547 --> 00:02:21.036
to complete the comparison. Mark them as unknown and

44
00:02:21.058 --> 00:02:24.436
identify how the responsible people can learn more. A

45
00:02:24.458 --> 00:02:27.413
sound recommendation can include an uncertainty and a next

46
00:02:27.436 --> 00:02:27.947
question.

47
00:02:28.978 --> 00:02:33.022
The Equity Analysis Toolkit's decision workspace can help organize

48
00:02:33.044 --> 00:02:37.578
alternatives, benefits, burdens, risks and evidence. Use the official

49
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.378
tool and any required process alongside it. Follow the

50
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.356
workspace's own instructions when saving to My Work or

51
00:02:44.378 --> 00:02:48.022
downloading notes; do not assume another worksheet saves information

52
00:02:48.044 --> 00:02:48.889
the same way.

53
00:02:49.389 --> 00:02:52.878
For a recommendation, explain why an option is being

54
00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:55.944
considered, what it would require and what could still

55
00:02:55.967 --> 00:02:59.189
go wrong. If people affected have not yet had

56
00:02:59.211 --> 00:03:02.856
a meaningful opportunity to inform an open choice, identify

57
00:03:02.878 --> 00:03:05.314
that gap and the next appropriate step.

58
00:03:05.814 --> 00:03:08.770
The aim is not to find a perfect answer

59
00:03:08.792 --> 00:03:12.081
in isolation. It is to make the reasoning clear

60
00:03:12.103 --> 00:03:14.726
enough for the people who hold the decision to

61
00:03:14.748 --> 00:03:17.970
weigh evidence, responsibilities and alternatives.

62
00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:22.868
In the activity below, compare proposed approaches to the

63
00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:26.157
reminder decision. Select the response that gives a reviewer

64
00:03:26.179 --> 00:03:29.179
the most useful basis for further work. Read the

65
00:03:29.201 --> 00:03:32.401
feedback after choosing, and compare the reasoning across the

66
00:03:32.423 --> 00:03:32.868
options.

67
00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:36.701
If you are using your own example, name at

68
00:03:36.723 --> 00:03:40.412
least two possible approaches and one possible benefit, burden

69
00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:43.657
or question for each. Keep the note general and

70
00:03:43.679 --> 00:03:45.279
free of confidential details.

71
00:03:46.832 --> 00:03:49.699
In the next lesson, we will bring the decision,

72
00:03:49.877 --> 00:03:54.388
information, alternatives and remaining questions together in a recommendation.

73
00:03:55.032 --> 00:03:57.232
The goal is a clear request for the appropriate

74
00:03:57.254 --> 00:04:00.388
review, not a statement that the change has already

75
00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.143
been approved.
